1
00:00:01,162 --> 00:00:05,993
A full walkthrough of all four workflows, start to finish.

2
00:00:05,993 --> 00:00:11,913
[Welcome] The sign-in screen. The live background reacts to the cursor, and the preview shows the product working.

3
00:00:11,913 --> 00:00:27,605
[Workflow 1 · Auth and enrollment] Register as a TA. Submitting an empty form shows the server’s Zod validation, field by field.

4
00:00:27,605 --> 00:00:30,674
[Workflow 1 · Auth and enrollment] Passwords are hashed with bcrypt. The session is a JWT in an httpOnly cookie.

5
00:00:30,674 --> 00:00:38,029
[Workflow 1 · Auth and enrollment] Meera has no courses yet. As a TA she can create one.

6
00:00:38,029 --> 00:00:42,650
[Workflow 1 · Auth and enrollment] The course gets a unique 6-character join code. It retries automatically if a code ever collides.

7
00:00:42,650 --> 00:00:54,044
[Meanwhile…] A co-TA and three classmates join with the code and start posting doubts.

8
00:00:54,044 --> 00:00:58,733
[Workflow 1 · Auth and enrollment] Refreshing shows 4 members now. Only the owner sees the member count and the join code.

9
00:00:58,733 --> 00:01:10,080
[Workflow 1 · Auth and enrollment] Now a student, Kabir, signs up and joins the course.

10
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:16,815
[Workflow 1 · Auth and enrollment] A wrong join code gets a clear 404 message…

11
00:01:16,815 --> 00:01:22,327
[Workflow 1 · Auth and enrollment] …and the right one enrolls him. Joining is a single atomic update, so it can never add him twice.

12
00:01:22,327 --> 00:01:26,458
[Workflow 3 · Browse, search, filter, upvote] The course queue, sorted by votes. It refreshes every 15 seconds while the tab is visible.

13
00:01:26,458 --> 00:01:33,145
[Workflow 3 · Browse, search, filter, upvote] Search uses a MongoDB text index, debounced while typing.

14
00:01:33,145 --> 00:01:35,703
[Workflow 3 · Browse, search, filter, upvote] Filter by status…

15
00:01:35,703 --> 00:01:40,810
[Workflow 3 · Browse, search, filter, upvote] …or sort by newest.

16
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:48,538
[Workflow 3 · Browse, search, filter, upvote] One upvote per user, as a toggle. The count updates instantly, then confirms with the server.

17
00:01:48,538 --> 00:01:56,392
[Workflow 2 · Duplicate detection] Kabir asks a doubt. As he types the title, similar doubts appear.

18
00:01:56,392 --> 00:02:02,614
[Workflow 2 · Duplicate detection] Matches are ranked by word overlap (Jaccard) plus character-trigram similarity, so near-matches still count.

19
00:02:02,614 --> 00:02:20,542
[Workflow 2 · Duplicate detection] It never blocks posting. His question is about a different case, so he posts anyway.

20
00:02:20,542 --> 00:02:25,731
[Workflow 2 · Duplicate detection] The doubt is open. Authors can’t upvote their own doubt, and only allowed actions are shown.

21
00:02:25,731 --> 00:02:37,117
[Workflow 4 · TA resolution flow] Back to Meera, the TA.

22
00:02:37,117 --> 00:02:42,192
[Workflow 4 · TA resolution flow] Two TAs can’t claim the same doubt. Watch: co-TA Rahul claims this one a moment before Meera does.

23
00:02:42,192 --> 00:02:47,360
[Workflow 4 · TA resolution flow] Her claim gets a 409: “Already claimed by Rahul Verma”. Claiming is one atomic findOneAndUpdate on status “open”.

24
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:50,413
[Workflow 4 · TA resolution flow] She claims Kabir’s doubt instead. The buttons come from permissions computed on the server.

25
00:02:50,413 --> 00:03:03,344
[Workflow 4 · TA resolution flow] Resolving needs at least one answer, so she writes one.

26
00:03:03,344 --> 00:03:14,886
[Workflow 4 · TA resolution flow] Resolved. The final answer is highlighted as accepted.

27
00:03:14,886 --> 00:03:20,217
[Workflow 4 · TA resolution flow] Only the author can reopen. Kabir still has a question, so he reopens it.

28
00:03:20,217 --> 00:03:24,086
[Workflow 4 · TA resolution flow] It goes back to open, with the answer kept. The status machine: open → claimed → resolved → open.

29
00:03:24,086 --> 00:03:32,273
[Details] Unknown routes get a friendly 404 page.

30
00:03:32,273 --> 00:03:37,489
Real output from the test suite and the race script.

31
00:03:37,489 --> 00:03:40,098
Thanks for watching!
